      "content": "While electrolytes can contribute to dizziness, self-treating potential medical symptoms should be approached with caution, especially at your age. Taking extra magnesium or increasing salt intake without medical direction might not be the best approach. Given the brief blackout and ongoing dizziness, the safest course of action is to contact your healthcare provider to discuss these symptoms. They can properly evaluate if it's dehydration, electrolyte imbalance, or something else needing attention.",
      "source": "target",
